 Two rules apply to every agent and to the orchestrator, through hooks and deny rules. Secrets are never read. AWS is never mutated directly: the guard allows only read-only AWS CLI operations, and every change goes through Terraform (human-applied) or an approved script.
 
+guard-dangerous.sh also blocks two command shapes for every caller, because it cannot see what bash would make of them. First, a backslash directly before a newline or carriage return, in any quote state. Second, `$'` or `$"` anywhere in a multi-line command or in a command that contains `${`, because a `#` comment or heredoc body can hide ANSI-C quoting from the guard. Put such commands on one line, or use the Write tool for file content.
